-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope of this license: third-party datasets in data/
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The BSD 3-Clause License above applies only to the original code of this
repository: everything outside the data/ directory.

It does NOT apply to the contents of data/. That directory holds benchmark
collections copied verbatim from other projects, and each keeps the license
under which its authors published it. Using or redistributing those files
means doing so under their own licenses, not under the license above. The
license text (or, where the upstream ships none, a NOTICE with the license
and the attribution) is kept beside each collection:

  data/maxima/
      Test files of Maxima (the Kamke and Murphy ODE collections, and the
      regression files for integrals, limits and algsys; Wester's problems
      released under the same license by their author).
      https://git.code.sf.net/p/maxima/code
      License:  GNU General Public License, version 2
      Text:     data/maxima/repository/COPYING
                data/maxima/repository/tests/wester_problems/
                  wester-gpl-permission-message.txt

  data/reduce/
      Test files of REDUCE (the ODESolve and DEFINT packages).
      https://github.com/reduce-algebra/reduce-algebra
      License:  Reduce License (BSD 2-clause style)
      Text:     data/reduce/LICENSE

  data/fricas/
      Input files of FriCAS (integ.input, mapleok.input).
      Copyright (c) 2007-2026 The FriCAS Team, 2002-2007 The Axiom Team,
      1991-2002 The Numerical Algorithms Group Ltd.
      https://github.com/fricas/fricas
      License:  modified BSD (3-clause)
      Text:     data/fricas/LICENSE.txt

  data/holpy/
      Integral examples of holpy. Copyright (c) 2018 bhzhan.
      https://github.com/bzhan/holpy
      License:  BSD 3-Clause
      Text:     data/holpy/LICENSE

  data/rocq-stdlib/
      The micromega test suite of the Rocq standard library.
      https://github.com/rocq-prover/stdlib
      License:  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
      Text:     data/rocq-stdlib/LICENSE

  data/mathlib4/
      Tactic tests of Lean's mathlib4.
      https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4
      License:  Apache License, version 2.0
      Text:     data/mathlib4/LICENSE

  data/tarski/
      Test inputs of Tarski. Copyright (c) 2015 Chris Brown.
      https://github.com/chriswestbrown/tarski
      License:  ISC-style permissive license
      Text:     data/tarski/interpreter/LICENSE

  data/qepcad/
      Regression tests and worked examples of QEPCAD B.
      Copyright (c) 1990, 2008 Hoon Hong & Chris Brown.
      https://github.com/chriswestbrown/qepcad
      License:  ISC-style permissive license
      Text:     data/qepcad/qesource/LICENSE

  data/bath-cad-examples/
      D. Wilson, Real Geometry and Connectedness via Triangular Description:
      CAD Example Bank, version 4, University of Bath Research Data
      Archive, 2013. https://researchdata.bath.ac.uk/69/
      License:  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
      Text:     data/bath-cad-examples/NOTICE

  data/solver-regressions-z3/
      Regression tests of Z3 (z3test). Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
      https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3test
      License:  MIT
      Text:     data/solver-regressions-z3/LICENSE.txt

  data/solver-regressions-cvc5/
      Regression tests of cvc5. Copyright (C) 2009-2026 by its authors and
      contributors. https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5
      License:  modified BSD (3-clause)
      Text:     data/solver-regressions-cvc5/COPYING

  data/meti-tarski/
      The Meti-Tarski family of the SMT-LIB 2025 release (non-incremental
      benchmarks), M. Preiner, H.-J. Schurr, C. Barrett, P. Fontaine,
      A. Niemetz, C. Tinelli. doi:10.5281/zenodo.16740866
      License:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
      Text:     data/meti-tarski/NOTICE

data/README.md lists the same collections with the upstream version each
copy was taken from.
